      'His words here come from a full-text OCR of a user-uploaded copy on the Internet Archive; quotes are kept short, normalized only for mechanical OCR glyph errors, and should be checked against a licensed print or ebook copy before wider publication. Page numbers were not available in that copy, so chapters are cited instead. The illustrations (the grape vine, the plant that is tired of soil, the appliance manual and warranty) are his teaching pictures, summarized here, not quoted. One phrase is weighed and corrected by the Word in the lesson: that we have the same components as God, and his line elsewhere in the chapter that we live forever by our own nature. The Word says man was formed from dust and given breath in Genesis 2:7, that Yahweh alone has immortality in 1 Timothy 6:16, and that eternal life is His gift in Romans 6:23. That correction is ours, made by the Word, and it strengthens rather than overturns his main point.',
