    bigIdea:
      'In The Burden of Freedom Dr. Myles Munroe spoke to post-colonial peoples, his own Bahamas first, and argued that being released from an oppressor is not the same as being free. Like Israel out of Egypt, a people can be delivered in body and still carry the conditioning of bondage in mind: fear, distrust, a hatred of work, an inability to manage. True freedom, he said, is the liberty to exercise dominion through your gifts in fulfillment of Yahweh’s purpose, and it is a burden only the mature can bear, because it demands responsibility and the renewing of the mind.',
